<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongolia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mongolian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mongolia is a region of steppe, mountains and desert in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. It was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of successive nomadic empires, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>. After the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>, Mongol rulers withdrew there, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> later brought it under its control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongolia.jpg" alt="Mongolia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Mongolia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
